WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.638
This episode focuses on economic programs.

2
00:00:02.638 --> 00:00:10.867
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:18.344
Business statistics describe establishments, firms, industries, employment, payroll, and receipts under program-specific rules.

4
00:00:18.344 --> 00:00:25.644
County Business Patterns covers establishments with paid employees and reports annual subnational data by industry and size.

5
00:00:25.644 --> 00:00:31.870
An establishment is a location where business activity occurs, while a firm may control multiple establishments.

6
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:35.705
Nonemployer Statistics covers many businesses without paid employees.

7
00:00:35.705 --> 00:00:39.707
Economic Census and annual programs have different frequency and detail.

8
00:00:39.707 --> 00:00:45.336
Industry classifications, suppression, reference years, and geographic coverage can change.

9
00:00:45.336 --> 00:00:50.594
Do not combine business counts with ACS worker estimates as if they share a universe.

10
00:00:50.594 --> 00:00:54.305
Use each program for the question it was designed to answer.

11
00:00:54.305 --> 00:00:55.900
Torrance application segment.

12
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.804
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

13
00:00:59.804 --> 00:01:06.788
The cited City of Torrance primary source is About Torrance, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/About-Torrance.

14
00:01:06.788 --> 00:01:15.531
For a local analysis, treat the City's description of its economy as local context and use federal business programs for reproducible establishment statistics.

15
00:01:15.531 --> 00:01:23.285
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

16
00:01:23.285 --> 00:01:33.238
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

17
00:01:33.238 --> 00:01:36.474
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

18
00:01:36.474 --> 00:01:41.237
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

19
00:01:41.237 --> 00:01:45.512
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

20
00:01:45.512 --> 00:01:51.496
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

21
00:01:51.496 --> 00:01:55.831
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
